                    <thead class="bg-neutral-light">
                        <tr><th class="p-4">Dimension</th><th class="p-4 text-primary">Lovart</th><th class="p-4">Nano Banana</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="divide-y divide-neutral/10">
                        <% comparisonRows.forEach(function(row) { %>
                        <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold"><%= row[0] %></td><td class="p-4"><%= row[1] %></td><td class="p-4"><%= row[2] %></td></tr>
                        <% }); %>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-10 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-5">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-950 mb-3">What Nano Banana Does</h2>
                <p class="text-amber-900 leading-relaxed">Nano Banana is handled here as a reported visual editing or image-model workflow. Without an official source in this execution, ownership, pricing, API access, and model version stay pending.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-neutral-light/40">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl space-y-12">
            <div>
                <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Best Use Cases</h2>
                <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">Use Lovart for connected design work: logos, brand kits, campaign assets, product shots, and video concepts. Use Nano Banana only where your current provider confirms the workflow you need, such as image editing, reference matching, or visual variation.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Image Editing and Consistency</h2>
                <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">Lovart official pages describe targeted editing, style consistency, and text edits. For Nano Banana, verify the specific interface, ownership, and model behavior before promising a consistent production workflow.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Brand Kit Workflow</h2>
                <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">Lovart is the safer first choice when the output must feel like a brand system rather than a single edited image. Continue to <a href="<%= link('/lovart-brand-kit') %>" class="text-primary font-semibold">Lovart Brand Kit</a> if your project needs colors, typography, logo direction, and related mockups.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Video and Campaign Assets</h2>
                <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">Lovart has official video generator pages. Still verify model access, export rights, credits, and account limits before selling video output to a client. Treat Nano Banana video claims as pending unless you have an official source.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Limits and Evidence</h2>
                <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">SERP snapshots, YouTube demos, Instagram reels, and third-party examples prove interest in the comparison, not feature truth. Any unverified Nano Banana capability remains reported or pending.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Video Evidence Status</h2>
            <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-5 text-amber-900">
                <p class="leading-relaxed">The 2026-07-14 report notes YouTube-type results for this query but does not provide specific video URLs. No video is embedded on this execution because adding a guessed URL would upgrade weak evidence into fabricated evidence.</p>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold">Evidence label: reported for video demand, pending for any specific video claim.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-neutral-light/40">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-5">Pricing and Access Checks</h2>
            <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed mb-5">Do not choose based on screenshots. Check whether your account can access the feature, what credits are consumed, whether exports include watermarking, and whether commercial use is allowed under the current terms.</p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                <a href="<%= link('/lovart-free') %>" class="px-5 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary text-white font-semibold">Lovart free guide</a>
                <a href="<%= link('/lovart-pricing') %>" class="px-5 py-3 rounded-lg border border-primary text-primary bg-white font-semibold">Lovart pricing guide</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-neutral/10">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-8">Lovart vs Nano Banana FAQ</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4">
                <details class="bg-neutral-light rounded-lg p-5"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Is Lovart better than Nano Banana?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-neutral">Only if you need a broader design-agent workflow. If your task is one specific image edit, verify the current Nano Banana tool before deciding.</p></details>
                <details class="bg-neutral-light rounded-lg p-5"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Does Lovart use Nano Banana?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-neutral">This remains disputed and pending in this execution. Public search results can show association or comparison demand, but they do not prove an official model relationship.</p></details>
                <details class="bg-neutral-light rounded-lg p-5"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Which is better for brand kits?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-neutral">Lovart is the safer comparison fit because official Lovart pages describe multi-asset design workflows and consistency features.</p></details>
                <details class="bg-neutral-light rounded-lg p-5"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Which is better for video ads?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-neutral">Lovart has official video generator pages. Nano Banana video claims should stay pending without official confirmation.</p></details>
                <details class="bg-neutral-light rounded-lg p-5"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Can I use the video examples as proof?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-neutral">No. Embedded videos are demand and workflow signals, not proof of product status, ownership, or pricing.</p></details>
                <details class="bg-neutral-light rounded-lg p-5"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">Is this page official?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-neutral">No. lovart.info is an independent guide site and is not affiliated with Lovart or Nano Banana.</p></details>
